module

public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.ProjRegrading
public import StacksFrontier.AlgebraicGeometry.Blowup.ReesGrading
public import StacksFrontier.RingTheory.Filtration.AssociatedGradedGrading

/-!
# The fibre of the Rees algebra over `V(I)` is the associated graded ring

Let `I` be an ideal of a commutative ring `A`. The Rees algebra `A[It] = ⨁_n Iⁿ` of `I` is graded
by `Stacks.Blowup.reesGrading`, and its base change along `A → A ⧸ I` is the associated graded
ring

```
(A ⧸ I) ⊗[A] A[It]  ≅  Gr_I(A) = ⨁_n Iⁿ/Iⁿ⁺¹
```

as graded rings, because `(A ⧸ I) ⊗[A] Iⁿ = Iⁿ/I·Iⁿ = Iⁿ/Iⁿ⁺¹`.

This is the algebraic content of the statement that the exceptional divisor of the blowup of
`Spec A` in `I` is `Proj` of the associated graded ring: the exceptional divisor is the fibre of
the blowup over the closed subscheme `V(I)`, which by base change for `Proj` is `Proj` of the
base-changed Rees algebra.

## Main definitions

* `Stacks.Blowup.grToTensor` is the comparison homomorphism `Gr_I(A) ⟶ (A ⧸ I) ⊗[A] A[It]`,
  built on the direct sum by `DirectSum.toSemiring`: the degree-`n` class of `x ∈ Iⁿ` is sent to
  `1 ⊗ monomial n x`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.reesToGr` is the `A`-linear map `A[It] ⟶ Gr_I(A)` taking the `n`-th coefficient
  of a Rees element to its class in `Iⁿ/Iⁿ⁺¹`, and `Stacks.Blowup.tensorToGr` is the `A`-linear
  map `(A ⧸ I) ⊗[A] A[It] ⟶ Gr_I(A)` it induces.
* `Stacks.Blowup.tensorEquivGr` is the resulting ring isomorphism
  `(A ⧸ I) ⊗[A] A[It] ≃+* Gr_I(A)`.
* `Stacks.Blowup.tensorGradedHomGr` and `Stacks.Blowup.grGradedHomTensor` are that isomorphism
  and its inverse as homomorphisms of graded rings, between the base-changed Rees grading and
  `AssociatedGraded.grading`.

## Main results

* `Stacks.Blowup.grToTensor_bijective`: the comparison homomorphism is bijective.
* `Stacks.Blowup.tensorGradedHomGr_comp` and `Stacks.Blowup.grGradedHomTensor_comp`: the two
  graded homomorphisms are mutually inverse.
* `Stacks.Blowup.irrelevant_le_map_tensorGradedHomGr` and
  `Stacks.Blowup.irrelevant_le_map_grGradedHomTensor`: the irrelevant-ideal hypotheses that
  `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.map` asks of them, so that `AlgebraicGeometry.Proj.isIso_map` applies
  to either and identifies `Proj ((A ⧸ I) ⊗[A] A[It])` with `Proj (Gr_I(A))`.

## Implementation notes

The isomorphism is constructed in the direction `Gr_I(A) ⟶ (A ⧸ I) ⊗[A] A[It]`, since a ring
homomorphism out of the external direct sum `Gr_I(A)` is given by `DirectSum.toSemiring`, which
asks only for the degreewise maps and for multiplicativity on homogeneous classes. Its inverse is
obtained by exhibiting a two-sided inverse of *additive* maps and appealing to
`RingEquiv.ofBijective`; no second multiplicativity argument is needed. The left inverse
`tensorToGr` is where the mathematical content sits: `Iⁿ ∋ x ↦ x mod Iⁿ⁺¹` kills `I · Iⁿ`
(`AssociatedGraded.smul_eq_zero_of_mem`), so it factors through the tensor product, and that is
exactly the injectivity of `(A ⧸ I) ⊗[A] Iⁿ → Iⁿ/Iⁿ⁺¹`.

The identification is the ring-level statement underlying Stacks tag 0AGQ part (1) and the
sentence in Section 51.22 (0GA6) reading `Y = Proj(⨁ Iⁿ/Iⁿ⁺¹)`: both are statements about
schemes — the exceptional divisor, resp. the fibre of the blowup over `V(I)`, is `Proj` of the
associated graded ring — obtained from this one by base change for `Proj` (tag 01N2).

No flatness hypothesis appears, and none is available: `A ⧸ I` is not a flat `A`-algebra, so
`Stacks.Blowup.reesBaseChangeEquiv` — which compares the Rees algebra of `I` with that of the
ideal generated by its image, and would here compare it with `reesAlgebra 0` — does not apply.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 0AGQ](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0AGQ) — part (1), whose proof
  uses this identification together with tag 00NO.
* [Stacks Project, Section 51.22 (0GA6)](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0GA6) — where the
  fibre of the blowup over `V(I)` is identified with `Proj` of the associated graded ring.
* [Stacks Project, Tag 0804](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0804) — the blowup of an affine
  as `Proj` of the Rees algebra.
* [Stacks Project, Section 15.4](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/07VD) — the associated
  graded ring.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

open Polynomial DirectSum TensorProduct AssociatedGraded HomogeneousIdeal

universe u

namespace Stacks.Blowup

variable {A : Type u} [CommRing A] (I : Ideal A)

/-! ### The monomials of the Rees algebra attached to the filtration -/

/-- The monomial `monomial n x`, for `x` in the `n`-th term `Iⁿ` of the `I`-adic filtration, as an
element of the Rees algebra. This is `Stacks.Blowup.reesMonomial` read on
`AssociatedGraded.power`. -/
def reesMonomialPow (n : ℕ) : (power (M := A) I n) →ₗ[A] reesAlgebra I :=
  (reesGrading I n).subtype ∘ₗ (reesMonomial I n ∘ₗ
    (LinearEquiv.ofEq _ _ (ring_power_eq I n)).toLinearMap)

/-- The underlying polynomial of `reesMonomialPow I n x` is `monomial n x`. -/
@[simp]
theorem coe_reesMonomialPow (n : ℕ) (x : power (M := A) I n) :
    ((reesMonomialPow I n x : reesAlgebra I) : A[X]) = monomial n (x : A) := by
  simp [reesMonomialPow]

/-- The monomial `reesMonomialPow I n x` is homogeneous of degree `n` for the Rees grading. -/
theorem reesMonomialPow_mem (n : ℕ) (x : power (M := A) I n) :
    reesMonomialPow I n x ∈ reesGrading I n :=
  (reesMonomial I n ((LinearEquiv.ofEq _ _ (ring_power_eq I n)) x)).2

/-- A homogeneous element of the Rees algebra of degree `n` is the monomial of its `n`-th
coefficient, which lies in the `n`-th term of the filtration. -/
theorem eq_reesMonomialPow_of_mem {n : ℕ} {f : reesAlgebra I} (hf : f ∈ reesGrading I n) :
    f = reesMonomialPow I n ⟨(f : A[X]).coeff n, by simpa using f.2 n⟩ :=
  Subtype.ext (coe_eq_monomial I hf)

/-- The monomial of degree zero attached to `1` is the unit of the Rees algebra. -/
theorem reesMonomialPow_zero_one (h : (1 : A) ∈ power (M := A) I 0) :
    reesMonomialPow I 0 ⟨1, h⟩ = 1 :=
  Subtype.ext (by simp)

/-- A tensor over the residue ring is a multiple of `1 ⊗ f`: the scalar is absorbed into the
Rees algebra. -/
theorem quotientMk_tmul (a : A) (f : reesAlgebra I) :
    (Ideal.Quotient.mk I) a ⊗ₜ[A] f = (1 : A ⧸ I) ⊗ₜ[A] (a • f) := by
  rw [TensorProduct.tmul_smul, TensorProduct.smul_tmul', Algebra.smul_def, mul_one,
    Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_eq]

/-! ### The comparison homomorphism out of the associated graded ring -/

/-- An element of the `(n+1)`-st term of the filtration, read inside the `n`-th, is a sum of
multiples by elements of `I` of elements of the `n`-th. -/
theorem mem_smul_top_of_coe_mem (n : ℕ) {x : power (M := A) I n}
    (hx : (x : A) ∈ power (M := A) I (n + 1)) :
    x ∈ I • (⊤ : Submodule A (power (M := A) I n)) := by
  have hmap : (I • (⊤ : Submodule A (power (M := A) I n))).map
      (Submodule.subtype (power (M := A) I n)) = power (M := A) I (n + 1) := by
    rw [Submodule.map_smul'', Submodule.map_top, Submodule.range_subtype, ring_power_eq,
      ring_power_eq, Ideal.smul_eq_mul, ← pow_succ']
  obtain ⟨y, hy, hyx⟩ : (x : A) ∈ (I • (⊤ : Submodule A (power (M := A) I n))).map
      (Submodule.subtype (power (M := A) I n)) := by rw [hmap]; exact hx
  exact Subtype.ext hyx ▸ hy

/-- **The degree-`n` comparison**: the class of `x ∈ Iⁿ` in `Iⁿ/Iⁿ⁺¹` is sent to the element
`1 ⊗ monomial n x` of the base change of the Rees algebra. It is well defined because `1 ⊗ a • y`
is `(a mod I) ⊗ y`, which vanishes for `a ∈ I`. -/
def pieceToTensor (n : ℕ) :
    piece (M := A) I n →ₗ[A] (A ⧸ I) ⊗[A] reesAlgebra I :=
  Submodule.liftQ _ ((TensorProduct.mk A (A ⧸ I) (reesAlgebra I) 1) ∘ₗ reesMonomialPow I n)
    (fun x hx => by
      refine Submodule.smul_induction_on (mem_smul_top_of_coe_mem I n hx) ?_ ?_
      · intro a ha y _
        simp only [LinearMap.mem_ker, map_smul, LinearMap.coe_comp, Function.comp_apply,
          TensorProduct.mk_apply]
        rw [TensorProduct.smul_tmul', Algebra.smul_def, mul_one, Ideal.Quotient.algebraMap_eq,
          (Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem).2 ha, TensorProduct.zero_tmul]
      · intro y z hy hz
        rw [LinearMap.mem_ker] at hy hz ⊢
        rw [map_add, hy, hz, add_zero])

/-- The class of `x ∈ Iⁿ` is sent by `pieceToTensor` to `1 ⊗ reesMonomialPow I n x`. -/
@[simp]
theorem pieceToTensor_mk (n : ℕ) (x : power (M := A) I n) :
    pieceToTensor I n (mk I n x) = 1 ⊗ₜ[A] reesMonomialPow I n x :=
  rfl

/-- **The comparison homomorphism `Gr_I(A) ⟶ (A ⧸ I) ⊗[A] A[It]`.** -/
def grToTensor : gradedRing I →+* (A ⧸ I) ⊗[A] reesAlgebra I :=
  DirectSum.toSemiring (fun n => (pieceToTensor I n).toAddMonoidHom)
    (by
      show pieceToTensor I 0 (mk I 0 ⟨1, by simp [power]⟩) = 1
      rw [pieceToTensor_mk, reesMonomialPow_zero_one, Algebra.TensorProduct.one_def])
    (by
      intro i j a b
      induction a using Quotient.inductionOn with
      | _ a =>
        induction b using Quotient.inductionOn with
        | _ b =>
          show (1 : A ⧸ I) ⊗ₜ[A] _ = ((1 : A ⧸ I) ⊗ₜ[A] _) * ((1 : A ⧸ I) ⊗ₜ[A] _)
          rw [Algebra.TensorProduct.tmul_mul_tmul, one_mul]
          congr 1
          exact Subtype.ext (by simp [monomial_mul_monomial]))

/-- On the degree-`n` class of `x ∈ Iⁿ`, `grToTensor` takes the value
`1 ⊗ reesMonomialPow I n x`. -/
@[simp]
theorem grToTensor_of (n : ℕ) (x : power (M := A) I n) :
    grToTensor I (DirectSum.of (fun k => piece (M := A) I k) n (mk I n x)) =
      1 ⊗ₜ[A] reesMonomialPow I n x :=
  DirectSum.toSemiring_of _ _ _ n _

/-! ### The inverse, as an additive map -/

/-- An element of `I` annihilates the associated graded ring. -/
theorem smul_gradedRing_eq_zero {a : A} (ha : a ∈ I) (z : gradedRing I) : a • z = 0 := by
  induction z using DirectSum.induction_on with
  | zero => simp
  | of n x =>
    rw [← DirectSum.of_smul, smul_eq_zero_of_mem I n ha x, map_zero]
  | add x y hx hy => rw [smul_add, hx, hy, add_zero]

/-- **The `A`-linear map `A[It] ⟶ Gr_I(A)`** taking a homogeneous Rees element of degree `n` to
the class of its `n`-th coefficient in `Iⁿ/Iⁿ⁺¹`. -/
def reesToGr : reesAlgebra I →ₗ[A] gradedRing I :=
  (DirectSum.toModule A ℕ (gradedRing I) fun n =>
      (DirectSum.lof A ℕ (fun k => piece (M := A) I k) n) ∘ₗ
        (Submodule.mkQ _) ∘ₗ
          ((LinearEquiv.ofEq _ _ (ring_power_eq I n)).symm.toLinearMap ∘ₗ
            (reesGradingEquivPow I n).symm.toLinearMap)) ∘ₗ
    (DirectSum.decomposeLinearEquiv (reesGrading I)).toLinearMap

/-- On a homogeneous Rees element `f` of degree `n`, `reesToGr` is the degree-`n` class of the
`n`-th coefficient of `f`. -/
theorem reesToGr_apply_of_mem {n : ℕ} {f : reesAlgebra I} (hf : f ∈ reesGrading I n) :
    reesToGr I f =
      DirectSum.of (fun k => piece (M := A) I k) n
        (mk I n ⟨(f : A[X]).coeff n, by simpa using f.2 n⟩) := by
  have h : f = ((⟨f, hf⟩ : reesGrading I n) : reesAlgebra I) := rfl
  rw [reesToGr, LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, h,
    DirectSum.decomposeLinearEquiv_apply_coe, DirectSum.toModule_lof]
  simp only [LinearMap.comp_apply, LinearEquiv.coe_coe, DirectSum.lof_eq_of, Submodule.mkQ_apply]
  refine congrArg (DirectSum.of (fun k => piece (M := A) I k) n) ?_
  exact congrArg (mk I n) (Subtype.ext (by simp))

/-- **The `A`-linear map `(A ⧸ I) ⊗[A] A[It] ⟶ Gr_I(A)`** induced by `Stacks.Blowup.reesToGr`:
the scalars act on the target through `A ⧸ I`, because `I` annihilates the associated graded
ring. -/
def tensorToGr : (A ⧸ I) ⊗[A] reesAlgebra I →ₗ[A] gradedRing I :=
  TensorProduct.lift (Submodule.liftQ I
    (LinearMap.toSpanSingleton A (reesAlgebra I →ₗ[A] gradedRing I) (reesToGr I))
    (fun a ha => LinearMap.mem_ker.2 (LinearMap.ext fun f => by
      simpa using smul_gradedRing_eq_zero I ha (reesToGr I f))))

/-- `tensorToGr` sends `1 ⊗ f` to `reesToGr I f`. -/
@[simp]
theorem tensorToGr_one_tmul (f : reesAlgebra I) :
    tensorToGr I (1 ⊗ₜ[A] f) = reesToGr I f := by
  rw [tensorToGr, TensorProduct.lift.tmul,
    show (1 : A ⧸ I) = Submodule.Quotient.mk (1 : A) from rfl, Submodule.liftQ_apply]
  simp

/-! ### The two maps are mutually inverse -/

/-- `tensorToGr` is a left inverse of `grToTensor`. -/
theorem tensorToGr_grToTensor (z : gradedRing I) : tensorToGr I (grToTensor I z) = z := by
  induction z using DirectSum.induction_on with
  | zero => simp
  | of n x =>
    induction x using Quotient.inductionOn with
    | _ x =>
      rw [show (Quotient.mk _ x : piece (M := A) I n) = mk I n x from rfl, grToTensor_of,
        tensorToGr_one_tmul, reesToGr_apply_of_mem I (reesMonomialPow_mem I n x)]
      refine congrArg (DirectSum.of (fun k => piece (M := A) I k) n) ?_
      exact congrArg (mk I n) (Subtype.ext (by simp))
  | add x y hx hy => rw [map_add, map_add, hx, hy]

/-- `grToTensor` sends `reesToGr I f` to `1 ⊗ f`. -/
theorem grToTensor_reesToGr (f : reesAlgebra I) :
    grToTensor I (reesToGr I f) = 1 ⊗ₜ[A] f := by
  classical
  rw [← DirectSum.sum_support_decompose (reesGrading I) f]
  rw [map_sum, map_sum, TensorProduct.tmul_sum]
  refine Finset.sum_congr rfl fun n _ => ?_
  set g : reesAlgebra I := ((DirectSum.decompose (reesGrading I) f n : reesGrading I n) :
    reesAlgebra I) with hg
  have hgmem : g ∈ reesGrading I n := (DirectSum.decompose (reesGrading I) f n).2
  rw [reesToGr_apply_of_mem I hgmem, grToTensor_of]
  exact congrArg _ (eq_reesMonomialPow_of_mem I hgmem).symm

/-- The comparison homomorphism `grToTensor : Gr_I(A) ⟶ (A ⧸ I) ⊗[A] A[It]` is bijective. -/
theorem grToTensor_bijective : Function.Bijective (grToTensor I) := by
  refine ⟨Function.LeftInverse.injective (tensorToGr_grToTensor I), fun w => ?_⟩
  induction w using TensorProduct.induction_on with
  | zero => exact ⟨0, map_zero _⟩
  | tmul c f =>
    obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective c
    exact ⟨reesToGr I (a • f), by rw [grToTensor_reesToGr, ← quotientMk_tmul]⟩
  | add x y hx hy =>
    obtain ⟨zx, hzx⟩ := hx
    obtain ⟨zy, hzy⟩ := hy
    exact ⟨zx + zy, by rw [map_add, hzx, hzy]⟩

/-- **The base change of the Rees algebra of `I` along `A → A ⧸ I` is the associated graded ring
of `I`.** -/
def tensorEquivGr : ((A ⧸ I) ⊗[A] reesAlgebra I) ≃+* gradedRing I :=
  (RingEquiv.ofBijective _ (grToTensor_bijective I)).symm

/-- The inverse of `tensorEquivGr` is `grToTensor`. -/
@[simp]
theorem tensorEquivGr_symm_apply (z : gradedRing I) :
    (tensorEquivGr I).symm z = grToTensor I z :=
  rfl

/-- `tensorEquivGr` sends `1 ⊗ f` to `reesToGr I f`. -/
@[simp]
theorem tensorEquivGr_one_tmul (f : reesAlgebra I) :
    tensorEquivGr I (1 ⊗ₜ[A] f) = reesToGr I f :=
  (tensorEquivGr I).symm.injective (by
    rw [RingEquiv.symm_apply_apply, tensorEquivGr_symm_apply, grToTensor_reesToGr])

/-! ### The comparison as homomorphisms of graded rings -/

/-- Every element of the degree-`n` part of the base change of the Rees algebra is `1 ⊗ f` for a
homogeneous `f` of degree `n`. -/
theorem exists_one_tmul_of_mem_baseChange {n : ℕ} {w : (A ⧸ I) ⊗[A] reesAlgebra I}
    (hw : w ∈ (reesGrading I n).baseChange (A ⧸ I)) :
    ∃ f : reesAlgebra I, f ∈ reesGrading I n ∧ w = 1 ⊗ₜ[A] f := by
  obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := Submodule.toBaseChange_surjective' _ _ hw
  clear hw
  induction x using TensorProduct.induction_on with
  | zero => exact ⟨0, zero_mem _, by simp⟩
  | tmul c g =>
    obtain ⟨a, rfl⟩ := Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective c
    exact ⟨a • (g : reesAlgebra I), Submodule.smul_mem _ _ g.2, by
      rw [Submodule.coe_toBaseChange_tmul, quotientMk_tmul]⟩
  | add x y hx hy =>
    obtain ⟨f, hf, hfx⟩ := hx
    obtain ⟨g, hg, hgy⟩ := hy
    refine ⟨f + g, add_mem hf hg, ?_⟩
    rw [map_add, Submodule.coe_add, hfx, hgy, TensorProduct.tmul_add]

/-- **The comparison, as a homomorphism of graded rings** from the base-changed Rees grading to
`AssociatedGraded.grading`. -/
def tensorGradedHomGr :
    (fun n => (reesGrading I n).baseChange (A ⧸ I)) →+*ᵍ grading I where
  __ := (tensorEquivGr I).toRingHom
  map_mem {n} {w} hw := by
    obtain ⟨f, hf, rfl⟩ := exists_one_tmul_of_mem_baseChange I hw
    rw [show (tensorEquivGr I).toRingHom (1 ⊗ₜ[A] f) = tensorEquivGr I (1 ⊗ₜ[A] f) from rfl,
      tensorEquivGr_one_tmul, reesToGr_apply_of_mem I hf]
    exact of_mem_grading I _

/-- **The inverse comparison, as a homomorphism of graded rings** from
`AssociatedGraded.grading` to the base-changed Rees grading. -/
def grGradedHomTensor :
    grading I →+*ᵍ fun n => (reesGrading I n).baseChange (A ⧸ I) where
  __ := (tensorEquivGr I).symm.toRingHom
  map_mem {n} {z} hz := by
    obtain ⟨x, rfl⟩ := hz
    induction x using Quotient.inductionOn with
    | _ x =>
      rw [show (tensorEquivGr I).symm.toRingHom _ = grToTensor I _ from rfl,
        show (Quotient.mk _ x : piece (M := A) I n) = mk I n x from rfl, grToTensor_of]
      exact Submodule.tmul_mem_baseChange_of_mem _ (reesMonomialPow_mem I n x)

/-- `grGradedHomTensor` is a left inverse of `tensorGradedHomGr`. -/
theorem grGradedHomTensor_comp :
    (grGradedHomTensor I).comp (tensorGradedHomGr I) =
      GradedRingHom.id fun n => (reesGrading I n).baseChange (A ⧸ I) :=
  GradedRingHom.ext fun w => (tensorEquivGr I).symm_apply_apply w

/-- `tensorGradedHomGr` is a left inverse of `grGradedHomTensor`. -/
theorem tensorGradedHomGr_comp :
    (tensorGradedHomGr I).comp (grGradedHomTensor I) = GradedRingHom.id (grading I) :=
  GradedRingHom.ext fun z => (tensorEquivGr I).apply_symm_apply z

/-- The irrelevant ideal of `AssociatedGraded.grading` is contained in the image under
`tensorGradedHomGr` of the irrelevant ideal of the base-changed Rees grading. -/
theorem irrelevant_le_map_tensorGradedHomGr :
    irrelevant (grading I) ≤
      (irrelevant fun n => (reesGrading I n).baseChange (A ⧸ I)).map (tensorGradedHomGr I) :=
  Stacks.GradedRegrading.irrelevant_le_map_of_comp_eq_id (tensorGradedHomGr_comp I)

/-- The irrelevant ideal of the base-changed Rees grading is contained in the image under
`grGradedHomTensor` of the irrelevant ideal of `AssociatedGraded.grading`. -/
theorem irrelevant_le_map_grGradedHomTensor :
    (irrelevant fun n => (reesGrading I n).baseChange (A ⧸ I)) ≤
      (irrelevant (grading I)).map (grGradedHomTensor I) :=
  Stacks.GradedRegrading.irrelevant_le_map_of_comp_eq_id (grGradedHomTensor_comp I)

end Stacks.Blowup

end
